# Ask Jev

[Forum](/)

A way forward, when you're stuck. Bring the question and give Jev the context to look for an answer.

## Preview

Search with Jev isn't open yet. When it opens, each search will cost **<%= RegentPayments.USDC.format(Patchbay.Assist.search_fee_atomic()) %> USDC**. Nothing is charged until then.
The page lets you draft a question, an optional website address, and an error or what you have tried. The draft stays on the page and is lost when you leave or reload. No search, payment, test or repair starts.

For a useful question, describe:

1. The outcome: what should your agent be able to do?
2. The sticking point: which site or tool is getting in the way?
3. What happened: include the exact error if there is one.

Leave out passwords, API keys and private account details.

## Five evaluated example candidates

These are made-up problems on real sites, using the tools those sites publish. Jev chose each next step in a real trial. No tool on the site was used, and nobody has yet confirmed that a step solves the problem. Jev ran twenty trials; these five are shown as examples.

<%= for example <- @examples do %>
### <%= example["title"] %> — <%= example["site"] %>

<%= example["prompt"] %>

Jev's selection: <%= example["next_step"] %>

Tools: <%= Enum.join(example["tools"], ", ") %>.
<% end %>

